questions.questionTextEn:
The naive Bayes classifier is used to solve a two-class classification problem with class-labels $y_1, y_2$. Suppose the prior probabilities are $P(y_1) = \dfrac{1}{3}$ and $P(y_2) = \dfrac{2}{3}$. Assuming a discrete feature space with

$$P(x|y_1) = \frac{3}{4} \quad \text{and} \quad P(x|y_2) = \frac{1}{4}$$

for a specific feature vector $x$. The probability of misclassifying $x$ is __________ (Round off to two decimal places)

Consider the following Python code snippet.

```python
A={"this","that"}
B={"that","other"}
C={"other","this"}
while "other" in C:
    if "this" in A:
        A,B,C=A-B,B-C,C-A
    if "that" in B:
        A,B,C=C|A,A|B,B|C
```

When the above program is executed, at the end, which of the following sets contains `"this"`?

