The division operator $\div$ finds every `customer_name` who has loans at ALL branches present in $\pi_{\text{branch\_name}}(\text{Loan}) = \{\text{Banjara Hills}, \text{Kondapur}, \text{SR Nagar}, \text{Balanagar}\}$. Checking each customer's branches:
- Anand: {Banjara Hills}
- Karteek: L11 (Banjara Hills), L14 (Kondapur), L22 (SR Nagar), L23 (Balanagar) $\to$ all 4 branches!
- Ankita: {SR Nagar}
- Gopal: {SR Nagar}
- Sunil: {Balanagar, Kondapur}
Only Karteek qualifies, so the query returns 1 tuple.

